Experiment 0011 - NOT FOR COMMIT. Rows for R16_* and R10G10B10A2_* in fd6_ubwc_compat_mode().

Why. In the stock fd6_ubwc_compat_mode() (src/freedreno/common/freedreno_ubwc.h)
there are 28 formats with a non-empty case, and among them there is not a single single-channel
16-bit one and not a single packed-10-bit one. Any format list into which
vkd3d puts R16 (and it always puts it, R16_TYPELESS and three more classes)
silently loses UBWC because of this.

Silently - because fd6_ubwc_compat_mode() returns
FD6_UBWC_UNKNOWN_COMPAT for them, and tu6_mutable_format_list_ubwc_compatible() exits with
false at the first unknown member. Then the !mutable_ubwc_fc branch clears
ubwc_enabled, and the image stays tiled but not compressed.

This is over-caution, not a hardware limitation, and it is measured, not derived.
The CEIL probe in tests/rp6-vkd3d-sparse-test.c (logs results/test-CEIL-base.log and
results/test-CEIL-exp0011.log) creates three images with one and the same list:
a linear one, the same format without a list, and that same one with MUTABLE. For a lone
R16_UNORM without a list the memreq comes to 0x82000 against linear 0x80000, i.e.
the UBWC metadata started on its own: the ceiling exists, and it is exactly the gate that
removes it.
The same for R10G10B10A2_UNORM: 0x102000 vs 0x100000.

Unlike experiment 0008, here one does not need to claim that the blob
"allows these, but not a660". Both formats are full-fledged in the texture path: in
fd6_format_table.c there is VTC(R16_UNORM, ..., WZYX) (line 72) and
FMT(R10G10B10A2_UNORM, ..., WZYX) at line 209, both have swap WZYX, i.e.
matching. The gap is only in the compat table, and this is exactly the case where
the argument "all variants of one block size differ only in the interpretation of
the same bits" holds fully: the layout depends only on the block size
(layout->cpp = util_format_get_blocksize(), fd6_layout.c:115), as in
0005/0006/0008, and the swap is shared by all members of the list.

What does NOT change. R8_* is deliberately not included here: it has no ceiling at all.
has_8bpp_ubwc = false on gen2 (freedreno_devices.py, working around the text corruption bug
from 0f770caa232, "Disable 8bpp_ubwc on a6xx gen2"), and the measurement confirms it -
the nonmemreq of a lone R8_UNORM equals the linear one. R32G32B32_* too: there are no
3-component rows in the blob and no ceiling is visible in measurements. These groups are blocked by
tu6_ubwc_possible(), not the gate, and they are not fixed by patching the rule.

Format name in the switch. The obvious name is wrong, and it cost one build:
VK_FORMAT_A2B10G10R10_UNORM_PACK32 maps to PIPE_FORMAT_R10G10B10A2_UNORM
(src/vulkan/util/vk_format.c:114), while PIPE_FORMAT_A2B10G10R10_UNORM never gets into this switch
at all, even though such a format exists in p_format.h. The cases hold
pipe names, not Vulkan ones.

What stays outside the experiment.
 - fast-clear: a byte roundtrip does not check the clear metadata, as in 0008.
 - reinterpretation through an R16_UINT view on an R16_TYPELESS list: exactly the
   mechanism that turned out broken in 0010 with diverging swaps. Here
   the swaps of all R16_* match (WZYX), so there will be no asymmetry, but
   it has to be tested separately.
 - Only R10G10B10A2_UNORM and _UINT are added to the compat row, because
   exactly they have tiled entries (FMT/VTC) in fd6_format_table.c; SNORM,
   SINT and USCALED have V__ there, i.e. no tiling. If vkd3d builds a list
   with SNORM or SINT, the question will already hit the texture format table rather than
   the gate, and the fix of this experiment will not be enough.

Measurement and analysis: docs/analysis.md, section 21.6.

diff --git a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_ubwc.h b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_ubwc.h
--- a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_ubwc.h
+++ b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_ubwc.h
@@ -26,6 +26,8 @@
    FD6_UBWC_R32G32_INT,
    FD6_UBWC_R32G32B32A32_INT,
    FD6_UBWC_R32_FLOAT,
+   FD6_UBWC_R16_INT,
+   FD6_UBWC_A2B10G10R10_INT,
 };
 
 static inline enum fd6_ubwc_compat_type
@@ -82,6 +84,35 @@
    case PIPE_FORMAT_R16G16B16A16_SINT:
       return FD6_UBWC_R16G16B16A16_INT;
 
+   case PIPE_FORMAT_R16_UNORM:
+   case PIPE_FORMAT_R16_SNORM:
+   case PIPE_FORMAT_R16_UINT:
+   case PIPE_FORMAT_R16_SINT:
+   case PIPE_FORMAT_R16_FLOAT:
+      /* EXPERIMENT - NOT FOR COMMIT.  The blob table has no single-channel
+       * 16-bit row at all, so every vkd3d list containing R16 (R16_TYPELESS and
+       * three more classes) silently loses UBWC.  Measured on a 740: a lone
+       * R16_UNORM image with no format list does get UBWC metadata
+       * (memreq 0x82000 vs 0x80000 linear), so the ceiling exists and the gate
+       * is what removes it.  All four variants are the same 16 bits read
+       * differently, and the tiled layout is a function of the block size
+       * alone (fd6_layout.c: layout->cpp = util_format_get_blocksize()).
+       */
+      return FD6_UBWC_R16_INT;
+
+   /* NB: vk_to_pipe_format() maps VK_FORMAT_A2B10G10R10_UNORM_PACK32 onto
+    * PIPE_FORMAT_R10G10B10A2_UNORM, not PIPE_FORMAT_A2B10G10R10_UNORM
+    * (src/vulkan/util/vk_format.c:114), so the R10G10B10A2 spelling is the
+    * one that actually reaches this switch. */
+   case PIPE_FORMAT_R10G10B10A2_UNORM:
+   case PIPE_FORMAT_R10G10B10A2_UINT:
+      /* Same argument for the packed 10-bit form, and the same measurement:
+       * a lone R10G10B10A2_UNORM image gets 0x102000 against 0x100000 linear.
+       * Only UNORM and UINT are added, and they are exactly the two with a
+       * tiled entry (VTC) in fd6_format_table.c; SNORM and SINT have none.
+       */
+      return FD6_UBWC_A2B10G10R10_INT;
+
    case PIPE_FORMAT_R32_UINT:
    case PIPE_FORMAT_R32_SINT:
       return FD6_UBWC_R32_INT;
